# The greenfield baseline's checksum is recorded in schema_migrations and is meant
# to be immutable and tamper-evident. scripts/schema-equivalence.mjs hashes the
# file's RAW BYTES, so without this pin a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true)
# would produce CRLF — and therefore a different digest than Linux/CI for
# byte-identical SQL, making the "immutable" checksum platform-dependent and
# defeating its purpose.
supabase/baseline/*.sql text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for the migration chain: several tests read these files and
# assert on their contents.
supabase/migrations/*.sql text eol=lf
